  "method_findings": [
    "Two source run folds per development ID; each of 20 TRAIN label shifts refits the entire supervised CSP4/LDA pipeline, predicting the unchanged holdout once. Exactly 40 fits per ID, 240 across six IDs, including 12 observed; no all40 model participates in fold fitting.",
    "Each cached fold prediction is crossed with all 20 holdout label shifts, yielding 400 joint rows per ID and 2400 overall; training shift and holdout shift use the same joint run-index pair in both folds. Synthetic test verifies exact equality to naive label-dependent refitting.",
    "Failed source fits retain explicit failure type/message, missing predictions and all 400 joint rows. Missing observed participant values prevent bootstrap aggregation. End receipt is written only after all six subjects finish; nonzero source fit failures produce completed_with_explicit_source_fit_failures, not unconditional success.",
    "Existing source40 arrays load with allow_pickle=False, exact before/after equality, source parameter hash, source40 IDs/X-y hash, and baseline full-GET receipt identities; these full40 models are never refitted.",
    "Support uses source-only StandardScaler on CSP4 features and unchanged source LDA score including intercept; class-specific signed margins, score bias, class recalls, class-collapse and strict-zero binary prediction boundary are preserved.",
    "Original and recomputed classwise support halves are retained under all 19/20 label rotations; zero-score-SD/single-class/zero-direction cases remain explicit. Positive direction cosine or signed-contrast product is not treated as a gate pass.",
    "No query/final roles are accepted by metadata validation; only development IDs 1,4,7,10,13,16, source ses0 runs0/1 and current support ses1..5 run0. Participant-unit bootstrap remains seed42 with10000 draws; no threshold/model selection is implemented."
  ],
